Summary of what I did and key findings:

- **Pulled the live schema** from Supabase (209 base tables in `public`, verbose with columns/PKs/FKs) and queried `pg_description` to enumerate the 27 tables and 64 columns that already had comments, so I could skip/avoid overwriting them.
- **Generated 182 `COMMENT ON TABLE`** statements (every base table except the 27 pre-commented ones) and **227 `COMMENT ON COLUMN`** statements for key columns only (loja_id FKs with the store-ID legend, status/tipo/categoria enums with values found in code, money columns, boolean flags, non-obvious FKs, snapshot columns, `*_por`/`*_by` user columns).
- **Validated programmatically**: no nonexistent table/column references, no duplicate statements, no overlap with pre-existing comments, every line is a well-formed `COMMENT` statement, and no unescaped apostrophes (none of the literals contain a `'`, so escaping is moot but verified).
- **Code-confirmed ambiguous tables**: `financial_records` is the DRE/P&L source (grupo/subgrupo de categoria); `agent_knowledge` = "Hermes" shared knowledge base between AI agents; `acoes_marketing.tipo_acao` values come from `Marketing.tsx` (Degustação, Cupom, Embaixador, Creator, Sócia, Evento, Brinde, Ação Promocional); `financial_entries`/`financial_accounts` appear legacy/unused (only in generated types) — flagged with `(?)`.
- **Uncertain tables flagged with `(?)`**: `active_review_sessions`, `logistica_events`, `financial_entries`, `financial_accounts`, `subscriptions` — described best-effort.
